<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Supplementary Technical Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Mutual Information Estimator</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, computing mutual information for high-dimensional embeddings in deep neural networks requires a statistical estimator.
We adopt the KSG estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kraskov et al., 2004</a>)</cite>, which relies on nearest-neighbor statistics to approximate the underlying probability densities:</p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}=\psi(k)-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\!\Bigl[\psi\bigl(n_{x}(i)+1\bigr)+\psi\bigl(n_{y}(i)+1\bigr)\Bigr]+\psi(n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>KSG</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}=\psi(k)-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\!\Bigl[\psi\bigl(n_{x}(i)+1\bigr)+\psi\bigl(n_{y}(i)+1\bigr)\Bigr]+\psi(n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is the fixed neighborhood size, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is the digamma function, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{x}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{x}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{y}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{y}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>) counts the number of samples, excluding <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, whose distance in the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) space is within the joint <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN radius <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Intuitively, the estimator measures how often neighbors in the joint space <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{1},Z_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{1},Z_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> also remain neighbors when projected to the marginal spaces, thereby capturing statistical dependence without explicitly estimating densities.
We further assume embeddings are bounded, i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z_{1,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z_{1,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z_{2,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z_{2,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring that distances and neighbor counts are well-defined.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Derivation of Utility Entropy</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the derivation of the Gaussian surrogate entropy used in the main content.
Consider a random variable <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with empirical covariance <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Among all continuous distributions with covariance <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gaussian distribution maximizes the differential entropy. Therefore, it is natural to approximate the empirical distribution of the embeddings by a zero mean Gaussian <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>. For a Gaussian random vector <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>, the differential entropy is given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(G)\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\log\bigl((2\pi e)^{d}\det(\Sigma)\bigr)=\tfrac{d}{2}\log(2\pi e)+\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det(\Sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(G)\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\log\bigl((2\pi e)^{d}\det(\Sigma)\bigr)=\tfrac{d}{2}\log(2\pi e)+\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det(\Sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When isotropic Gaussian noise <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math> is added to <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulting distribution is <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma+\sigma^{2}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma+\sigma^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Its entropy is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathrm{G}}(X+Z)\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\log\bigl((2\pi e)^{d}\det(\Sigma+\sigma^{2}I)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathrm{G}}(X+Z)\;=\;\tfrac{1}{2}\log\bigl((2\pi e)^{d}\det(\Sigma+\sigma^{2}I)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Subtracting the clean entropy <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathrm{G}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathrm{G}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H_{\mathrm{util}}(\sigma)=H_{\mathrm{G}}(X+Z)-H_{\mathrm{G}}(X)=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det\!\Bigl(I+\tfrac{\sigma^{2}I}{\Sigma}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>util</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.177em;" width="1.177em"><mo movablelimits="false">det</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H_{\mathrm{util}}(\sigma)=H_{\mathrm{G}}(X+Z)-H_{\mathrm{G}}(X)=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det\!\Bigl(I+\tfrac{\sigma^{2}I}{\Sigma}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This expression quantifies the increase in entropy introduced by Gaussian perturbation. Since higher entropy indicates less structure and more randomness, a smaller <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H_{\mathrm{util}}(\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>util</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H_{\mathrm{util}}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to better preservation of the informative content of the original embeddings.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Derivation of Verification Entropy</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hypothesis testing setup.</span>
The verification problem is cast as a binary hypothesis test:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\begin{cases}\mathrm{ind},&amp;\text{if the queried model is independent of the protected model},\\
\mathrm{sur},&amp;\text{if the queried model is a surrogate trained with at most $Q$ queries}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ind</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if the queried model is independent of the protected model</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>sur</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if the queried model is a surrogate trained with at most </mtext><mi>Q</mi><mtext> queries</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\begin{cases}\mathrm{ind},&amp;\text{if the queried model is independent of the protected model},\\
\mathrm{sur},&amp;\text{if the queried model is a surrogate trained with at most $Q$ queries}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Given a sample set <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> queries, the verifier computes the empirical mutual information statistic <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. The indicator is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T_{\sigma}=\mathbf{1}\{\widehat{I}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\sigma}=\mathbf{1}\{\widehat{I}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary random variable indicating the verifier’s choice, and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(\sigma,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(\sigma,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> is a threshold that may depend on the noise parameter <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and query budget <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error probabilities.</span>
We have two types of error,
<span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Independent False Alarm (Type I error)</span>: <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[T_{\sigma}=1\mid H=\mathrm{ind}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ind</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[T_{\sigma}=1\mid H=\mathrm{ind}]</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., incorrectly declaring the model a surrogate.
<span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Surrogate Missed Detection (Type II error)</span>: <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[T_{\sigma}=0\mid H=\mathrm{sur}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sur</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[T_{\sigma}=0\mid H=\mathrm{sur}]</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., failing to detect a surrogate. By concentration bounds for empirical mutual information, these probabilities can be bounded as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[T_{\sigma}=1\mid H=\mathrm{ind}]\leq\gamma_{1}(\sigma,Q)=\exp\!\Bigl(-\tfrac{2|\mathcal{S}|\,\tau(\sigma,Q)^{2}}{C^{2}}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ind</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[T_{\sigma}=1\mid H=\mathrm{ind}]\leq\gamma_{1}(\sigma,Q)=\exp\!\Bigl(-\tfrac{2|\mathcal{S}|\,\tau(\sigma,Q)^{2}}{C^{2}}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr[T_{\sigma}=0\mid H=\mathrm{sur}]\leq\gamma_{2}(\sigma,Q)=\exp\!\Bigl(-\tfrac{2|\mathcal{S}|\,\bigl(I_{\ast}(\sigma,Q)-\tau(\sigma,Q)\bigr)^{2}}{C^{2}}\Bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sur</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[T_{\sigma}=0\mid H=\mathrm{sur}]\leq\gamma_{2}(\sigma,Q)=\exp\!\Bigl(-\tfrac{2|\mathcal{S}|\,\bigl(I_{\ast}(\sigma,Q)-\tau(\sigma,Q)\bigr)^{2}}{C^{2}}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a bound on the range of the score function and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\ast}(\sigma,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\ast}(\sigma,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> is the population mutual information under the surrogate model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verification entropy.</span>
Let <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{0}=\Pr[H=\mathrm{ind}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ind</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}=\Pr[H=\mathrm{ind}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{1}=\Pr[H=\mathrm{sur}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sur</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=\Pr[H=\mathrm{sur}]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the prior probabilities. The conditional entropy of the decision <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma)=\pi_{0}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\Pr[T_{\sigma}=1\mid H=\mathrm{ind}]\bigr)+\pi_{1}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\Pr[T_{\sigma}=0\mid H=\mathrm{sur}]\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>ver</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ind</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>sur</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma)=\pi_{0}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\Pr[T_{\sigma}=1\mid H=\mathrm{ind}]\bigr)+\pi_{1}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\Pr[T_{\sigma}=0\mid H=\mathrm{sur}]\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma)=\pi_{0}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\gamma_{1}(\sigma,Q)\bigr)+\pi_{1}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\gamma_{2}(\sigma,Q)\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>ver</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma)=\pi_{0}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\gamma_{1}(\sigma,Q)\bigr)+\pi_{1}\,h_{b}\!\bigl(\gamma_{2}(\sigma,Q)\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{b}(p)=-p\log p-(1-p)\log(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{b}(p)=-p\log p-(1-p)\log(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary entropy function. In practice, if no prior knowledge about <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is available, it is common to assume a uniform prior <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}=\pi_{1}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}=\pi_{1}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the noiseless setting (<math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0</annotation></semantics></math>), the test achieves perfect accuracy, so <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>ver</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">verification entropy gain</em> is then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma)=\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>ver</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>ver</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma)=\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{ver}}(\sigma).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This formulation makes clear that the entropy grows as error probabilities increase, quantifying the loss of verification robustness introduced by Gaussian perturbation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h3>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gaussian Mechanism)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathcal{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathcal{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a query and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a noise scale parameter. The <em id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gaussian mechanism</em> <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}(X)\;=\;f(X)+Z,\qquad\text{where }Z\sim\mathcal{N}\!\bigl(0,\,\sigma^{2}I_{d}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}(X)\;=\;f(X)+Z,\qquad\text{where }Z\sim\mathcal{N}\!\bigl(0,\,\sigma^{2}I_{d}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This mechanism provides differential privacy based on the global <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> sensitivity of the query, defined as
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}=\sup_{x,x^{\prime}}\|f(x)-f(x^{\prime})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}=\sup_{x,x^{\prime}}\|f(x)-f(x^{\prime})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
To ensure that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>-differential privacy for given <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the noise scale <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> must be chosen to meet the following condition:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\;\geq\;\frac{\sqrt{2\,\ln\!\bigl(1.25/\delta\bigr)}\,\Delta_{2}}{\epsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1.25</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\;\geq\;\frac{\sqrt{2\,\ln\!\bigl(1.25/\delta\bigr)}\,\Delta_{2}}{\epsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mutual Information Bound for the Gaussian Mechanism)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a function with global <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> sensitivity <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the Gaussian mechanism <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}(X)=f(X)+Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}(X)=f(X)+Z</annotation></semantics></math>, where the noise <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the input <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. The mutual information between the input <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and the output <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;e_{g}(X))\leq\frac{\Delta^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;e_{g}(X))\leq\frac{\Delta^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Data Processing Inequality, DPI)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any random variables forming a Markov chain <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\to Y\to Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\to Y\to Z</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> are conditionally independent given <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, the mutual information satisfies:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;Z)\leq I(X;Y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;Z)\leq I(X;Y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Markov Chain from a Common Ancestor)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a random variable. Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=e_{h}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=e_{h}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=e_{g}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=e_{g}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> be two random variables generated from <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> via two (possibly randomized) functions, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the random variables <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y,X,Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y,X,Z</annotation></semantics></math> form a Markov chain <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\to X\to Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\to X\to Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Markov Chain from a Common Ancestor). ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\to X\to Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\to X\to Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a Markov chain, we must show that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> are conditionally independent given <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(Y,Z|X=x)=P(Y|X=x)P(Z|X=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(Y,Z|X=x)=P(Y|X=x)P(Z|X=x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, the generation of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> (via mechanism <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>), and the generation of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> (via mechanism <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>). Once the value of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, the two generation processes are independent of each other. Therefore, their conditional joint probability factors into the product of their conditional marginal probabilities, establishing the Markov chain.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mutual Information Bound Between Two Privatized Outputs)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a random variable, and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=e_{h}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=e_{h}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=e_{g}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=e_{g}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. If the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Gaussian mechanism, then the mutual information between <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;Z)\leq\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;Z)\leq\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Mutual Information Bound). ‣ 3.1 Building Defense Model via a Gaussian Mechanism ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Markov Chain from a Common Ancestor). ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have established that the random variables form the Markov chain <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\to X\to Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\to X\to Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Data Processing Inequality (Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3 (Data Processing Inequality, DPI). ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>), this Markov chain implies:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))\leq I(X;e_{g}(X))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))\leq I(X;e_{g}(X)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (Mutual Information Bound for the Gaussian Mechanism). ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Appendix B Proofs ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, since <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> is gaussian mechanism, we have the bound:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;e_{g}(X))\leq\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;e_{g}(X))\leq\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these two inequalities yields the desired result in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Mutual Information Bound). ‣ 3.1 Building Defense Model via a Gaussian Mechanism ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))\leq\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))\leq\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem 2</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Tightness). ‣ 3.1 Building Defense Model via a Gaussian Mechanism ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Construction.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\{x_{0},x_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\{x_{0},x_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}(x_{0})=P_{X}(x_{1})=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}(x_{0})=P_{X}(x_{1})=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(x_{0})=-\Delta_{2}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{0})=-\Delta_{2}/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(x_{1})=+\Delta_{2}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{1})=+\Delta_{2}/2</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f(x_{0})-f(x_{1})\|_{2}=\Delta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f(x_{0})-f(x_{1})\|_{2}=\Delta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}(x)=f(x)+Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}(x)=f(x)+Z</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{h}(X)=X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{h}(X)=X</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))=I(X;e_{g}(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))=I(X;e_{g}(X))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Binary Gaussian channel form.<span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Then</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{g}(X)\sim\begin{cases}\mathcal{N}(-\Delta_{2}/2,\;\sigma^{2})&amp;\text{w.p. }\tfrac{1}{2},\\[2.0pt]
\mathcal{N}(+\Delta_{2}/2,\;\sigma^{2})&amp;\text{w.p. }\tfrac{1}{2}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>w.p. </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>w.p. </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{g}(X)\sim\begin{cases}\mathcal{N}(-\Delta_{2}/2,\;\sigma^{2})&amp;\text{w.p. }\tfrac{1}{2},\\[2.0pt]
\mathcal{N}(+\Delta_{2}/2,\;\sigma^{2})&amp;\text{w.p. }\tfrac{1}{2}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define the parameter <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\triangleq 1/\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\triangleq 1/\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the standard normalization, write
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=f(X)+Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=f(X)+Z</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, so by scaling,
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Y}=\sqrt{s}\,f(X)+N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Y}=\sqrt{s}\,f(X)+N</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lower bound via the <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>–MMSE relation.<span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
For any real <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;\sqrt{t}\,X+N)=\tfrac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathrm{mmse}(u)\,du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>mmse</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;\sqrt{t}\,X+N)=\tfrac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{t}\mathrm{mmse}(u)\,du</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2005</a>)</cite>.
Take <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=s</annotation></semantics></math> and note <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(f(X))=\Delta_{2}^{2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(f(X))=\Delta_{2}^{2}/4</annotation></semantics></math> for our symmetric binary <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.
It is known that <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{mmse}(u)=\mathrm{Var}(f(X))-O(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>mmse</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{mmse}(u)=\mathrm{Var}(f(X))-O(u)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>; hence there exists <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{mmse}(u)\geq\mathrm{Var}(f(X))-C_{0}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>mmse</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{mmse}(u)\geq\mathrm{Var}(f(X))-C_{0}u</annotation></semantics></math>
for all small <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;e_{g}(X))\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{s}\mathrm{mmse}(u)\,du\;\geq\;\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{s}\left(\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{4}-C_{0}u\right)du\;=\;\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8}\,s\;-\;\frac{C_{0}}{4}\,s^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>mmse</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;e_{g}(X))\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{s}\mathrm{mmse}(u)\,du\;\geq\;\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{s}\left(\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{4}-C_{0}u\right)du\;=\;\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8}\,s\;-\;\frac{C_{0}}{4}\,s^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1/\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1/\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\Delta_{2}^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\Delta_{2}^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8}\,s=\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8}\cdot\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}=\frac{1}{4}\,\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}=\frac{\beta}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8}\,s=\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{8}\cdot\frac{1}{\sigma^{2}}=\frac{1}{4}\,\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}=\frac{\beta}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C_{0}}{4}\,s^{2}=\frac{C_{0}}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{\sigma^{4}}=\underbrace{\frac{C_{0}}{\Delta_{2}^{4}}}_{\triangleq C}\,\left(\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)^{\!2}=C\,\beta^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C_{0}}{4}\,s^{2}=\frac{C_{0}}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{\sigma^{4}}=\underbrace{\frac{C_{0}}{\Delta_{2}^{4}}}_{\triangleq C}\,\left(\frac{\Delta_{2}^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)^{\!2}=C\,\beta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;e_{g}(X))\;\geq\;\frac{\beta}{4}-C\,\beta^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;e_{g}(X))\;\geq\;\frac{\beta}{4}-C\,\beta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion.<span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Since <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\beta^{2}=o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\beta^{2}=o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))=I(X;e_{g}(X))\geq\tfrac{\beta}{4}-o(\beta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))=I(X;e_{g}(X))\geq\tfrac{\beta}{4}-o(\beta).</annotation></semantics></math>
Therefore the upper bound <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(e_{h}(X);e_{g}(X))\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is tight up to a universal constant factor, establishing order-wise tightness.
∎</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Theorem 3</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (Certified Ownership Verification Guarantee). ‣ 3.2 Certified Verification Threshold ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> (Type I Error).</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}\triangleq\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}\!\bigl(e_{h_{\mathrm{ind}}}(X),e_{g}(X)\bigr),\qquad\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\triangleq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{I}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>KSG</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}\triangleq\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}\!\bigl(e_{h_{\mathrm{ind}}}(X),e_{g}(X)\bigr),\qquad\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\triangleq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{I}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Estimator.<span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We use the KSG estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kraskov et al., 2004</a>)</cite>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}=\psi(k)-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\!\Bigl[\psi\bigl(n_{x}(i)+1\bigr)+\psi\bigl(n_{y}(i)+1\bigr)\Bigr]+\psi(n)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>KSG</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}=\psi(k)-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\!\Bigl[\psi\bigl(n_{x}(i)+1\bigr)+\psi\bigl(n_{y}(i)+1\bigr)\Bigr]+\psi(n),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is the digamma function, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{x}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{x}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of samples (excluding <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>) whose <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-distance to sample <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> does not exceed the joint <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN radius <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{y}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{y}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined analogously in <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> space. Assume embeddings are bounded: <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z_{1,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z_{1,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z_{2,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z_{2,i}\|_{2}\leq B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so all distances and counts are well-defined.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounded differences.<span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Replace a single sample <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{1,r},Z_{2,r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{1,r},Z_{2,r})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z^{\prime}_{1,r},Z^{\prime}_{2,r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z^{\prime}_{1,r},Z^{\prime}_{2,r})</annotation></semantics></math>. This can affect:
(i) the <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-th summand itself,
(ii) any sample <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq r</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> falls inside the ball of radius <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (thus changing <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{x}(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{x}(j)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{y}(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{y}(j)</annotation></semantics></math> by at most <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>).
For <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-nearest neighbour type estimators, each point can belong to at most <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> such neighbour sets in each marginal space, so at most <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k</annotation></semantics></math> other summands change. Hence, no more than <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k+1)</annotation></semantics></math> summands are affected. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone and for <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in[1,n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in[1,n]</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\psi(m_{1})-\psi(m_{2})|\leq\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\psi(m_{1})-\psi(m_{2})|\leq\log n</annotation></semantics></math>, each affected summand</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(n_{x}(i)+1)+\psi(n_{y}(i)+1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(n_{x}(i)+1)+\psi(n_{y}(i)+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">changes by at most <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\log n</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore the total change in the average is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\widehat{I}-\widehat{I}^{\prime}\bigr|\leq\frac{(2k+1)\cdot 2\log n}{n}=\frac{C_{k}}{n},\qquad C_{k}\triangleq 2(2k+1)\log n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\widehat{I}-\widehat{I}^{\prime}\bigr|\leq\frac{(2k+1)\cdot 2\log n}{n}=\frac{C_{k}}{n},\qquad C_{k}\triangleq 2(2k+1)\log n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus McDiarmid’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">McDiarmid and others, 1989</a>)</cite> applies with <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=C_{k}/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=C_{k}/n</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Applying McDiarmid (upper tail).<span id="A2.SS3.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
For any <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\widehat{I}-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\geq t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}(c_{i})^{2}}\right)=\exp\!\left(-\frac{2nt^{2}}{C_{k}^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\widehat{I}-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\geq t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}(c_{i})^{2}}\right)=\exp\!\left(-\frac{2nt^{2}}{C_{k}^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\tau(\sigma,Q)-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\tau(\sigma,Q)-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By design (independently trained <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathrm{ind}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathrm{ind}}</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}&lt;\tau(\sigma,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}&lt;\tau(\sigma,Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\bigl(\tau(\sigma,Q)-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\bigr)^{2}}{C_{k}^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\bigl(\tau(\sigma,Q)-\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\bigr)^{2}}{C_{k}^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">In the ideal case <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ind</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{ind}}\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math> (true MI near zero and KSG is consistent), this becomes</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\,\tau(\sigma,Q)^{2}}{\bigl[2(2k+1)\log n\bigr]^{2}}\right)\triangleq\gamma_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\,\tau(\sigma,Q)^{2}}{\bigl[2(2k+1)\log n\bigr]^{2}}\right)\triangleq\gamma_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is the stated Type I bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (Certified Ownership Verification Guarantee). ‣ 3.2 Certified Verification Threshold ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> (Type II Error).</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}\triangleq\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}\!\bigl(e_{h_{\mathrm{sur}}}(X),e_{g}(X)\bigr),\qquad\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}\triangleq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{I}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>KSG</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}\triangleq\widehat{I}_{\mathrm{KSG}}\!\bigl(e_{h_{\mathrm{sur}}}(X),e_{g}(X)\bigr),\qquad\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}\triangleq\mathbb{E}[\widehat{I}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">We again use the KSG estimator with the same bounded embedding and i.i.d. sample assumptions as in the Type I proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounded differences.<span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The identical argument shows that replacing a single sample changes <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}</annotation></semantics></math> by at most <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}/n</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}=2(2k+1)\log n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}=2(2k+1)\log n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Applying McDiarmid (lower tail).<span id="A2.SS3.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We want</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}\leq\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]=\Pr\!\left[\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\widehat{I}\geq\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}\leq\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]=\Pr\!\left[\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\widehat{I}\geq\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\tau(\sigma,Q)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Assume the surrogate is sufficiently close to <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}&gt;\tau(\sigma,Q)</annotation></semantics></math>; set <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\tau(\sigma,Q)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\tau(\sigma,Q)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. McDiarmid’s inequality yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}\leq\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\,t^{2}}{C_{k}^{2}}\right)=\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\bigl(\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\tau(\sigma,Q)\bigr)^{2}}{\bigl[2(2k+1)\log n\bigr]^{2}}\right)\triangleq\gamma_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left[\widehat{I}\leq\tau(\sigma,Q)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\,t^{2}}{C_{k}^{2}}\right)=\exp\!\left(-\frac{2n\bigl(\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}-\tau(\sigma,Q)\bigr)^{2}}{\bigl[2(2k+1)\log n\bigr]^{2}}\right)\triangleq\gamma_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(\sigma,Q)\to\beta(\sigma,\delta)(1-\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(\sigma,Q)\to\beta(\sigma,\delta)(1-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>sur</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{sur}}</annotation></semantics></math> stays above this limit by a positive margin, the exponent diverges to <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{2}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{2}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Reproducibility</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Dataset Statistics</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides an overview of the datasets used across different modalities. For the image classification tasks, we employ most commonly used CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100, with detailed statistics summarized in Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ C.1 Dataset Statistics ‣ Appendix C Reproducibility ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A3.T4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Statistics of commonly used real-world image classification datasets.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A3.T4.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T4.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Dataset</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Classes</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.7.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">#Images</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.7.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Train / Test Split</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.7.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Resolution</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T4.7.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.7.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">CIFAR-10</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.7.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.7.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">60,000</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.7.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">50,000 / 10,000</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.7.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><math id="A3.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.800em">32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T4.7.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> RGB</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.7.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.7.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">CIFAR-100</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.7.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">100</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.7.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">60,000</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.7.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A3.T4.7.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">50,000 / 10,000</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.7.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.45pt 5.0pt;"><math id="A3.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.800em">32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.T4.7.3.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> RGB</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the graph classification tasks, we employ most commonly used ENZYMES and PROTEINS datasets, with their corresponding statistics reported in Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ C.1 Dataset Statistics ‣ Appendix C Reproducibility ‣ CREDIT: Certified Ownership Verification of Deep Neural Networks Against Model Extraction Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A3.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A3.T5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Statistics of commonly used real-world graph classification datasets.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A3.T5.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
